From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:26:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - route entity-owned bridge callbacks

Carry the callback's entity target into the bridge. A sync callback
wrapped in EntityTask runs on the region owning the entity when due and
is cancelled as a rejected operation if the entity is removed first.
Explicit global and async requests do not consult it.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
index bd31b28d155c5a5a51b284ffc51384cfe0100085..673dc72cb29a18b6cb7d664614c91fb66112d525 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
@@ -563,6 +563,9 @@ public class CraftScheduler implements BukkitScheduler {
             @Override public dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.execution.region.RegionAnchor targetRegion() {
                 return dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.bridge.AuroraBridge.targetRegion(task.getOwner(), task.rTask);
             }
+            @Override public Object targetEntity() {
+                return dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.bridge.AuroraBridge.targetEntity(task.getOwner(), task.rTask);
+            }
             @Override public long period() { return task.getPeriod(); }
             @Override public boolean cancelled() { return task.isCancelled(); }
             @Override public void markCancelled() {
